.TH DQL-SERVER 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-server \- serve the DelightQL relay protocol on a Unix socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a relay-protocol server on a Unix domain socket. On startup the
socket path is printed alone on the first stdout line (convenient for
scripts), followed by a human-readable status line naming the worker
count, database, and timeouts. This is the execution backend used by
the project's internal test tooling.
.SH PROTOCOL
The relay protocol is an
.B internal detail exposed as a subcommand
\(em a framed binary protocol that
.B carries no compatibility promise.
A bare text write to the socket (e.g. via
.BR nc )
receives no reply by design: sessions begin with a version handshake,
and the frame format may change between releases without notice.
.PP
The protocol is not unspecified \(em it follows a draft logical\-model
specification (the SQL9 relay\-protocol documents in the
.B delightql\-protocol
crate of the source tree), whose long\-term ambition is a public,
content\-blind contract for moving relations between processes. Until
that specification is ratified, it remains Draft and the protocol
remains internal: nothing about today's frames is promised.
.PP
For programmatic use today, the supported surfaces are the CLI
.RB ( "dql query \-f json"
with
.BR "\-\-error\-format json" ,
structured errors on stderr) and the C\-ABI embedding.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Unix socket path. Default:
.IR /tmp/dql\-{pid}.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of worker threads. Default 0 = available CPUs.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
Shut down after N seconds with no messages. 0 (default) disables.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
Shut down after N seconds with zero active connections. 0 (default)
disables.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " DATABASE"
SQLite database file; default is in-memory (shown as
.IR db=<none> ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on clean shutdown (including timeout-triggered shutdown).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a self-reaping server for a scripted session:
.PP
.EX
$ sock=$(dql server --socket-idle-timeout 30 | head -1)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql\-query (1),
.BR dql\-target (1)
